# q2-usbtrace trace format (docs/internals.md#usb-tracer), built from a device log for test/unit/test_usb_fsm.py.
# Source: usbprobe/usblog2.txt, 2026-11-25, the owner's plugs, unified log lines (uptime ms as s; the kernel's and
# demo's share the clock), on the trunk's 3 s settle. Measured: the cable out at 830.614 and PD18 low by its out+5s
# line (835.673), otg-on 843.921, otg-trial-off 852.884, wrong-role 855.917 (a laptop the wrong way round); a computer
# in at 3211.629, out 4488.311, in 4498.375, out 4508.636; USB-C headphones: otg-on 4583.606, the kernel's errors for
# "usb 1-1.1" (behind a hub in the headphones) at 4586.084 and "Not connected", otg-off why=gone 4587.327; a laptop
# the wrong way round again: otg-on 4605.614, otg-off why=id-high 4611.579 (2 s of ID high, OTG_ID_HIGH_MS, so high
# by 4609.579), its cable seen in at 4619.123. Not in the log: when each ID low began (put at the out+5s line for the
# first, which may be late, and 3 s before otg-on, the settle, for the others) [I]; the hub's 1-1 add (put 0.56 s after
# otg-on, as 2026-11-23 measured [E]) and its removal (put 50 ms before otg-off why=gone) [I]; online (1 with a
# computer's or the laptop's VBUS in, else 0) [I]; a computer's address (put at its in+5s line, so its "charger" at
# 3 s is the log's resolution, not the computer's) [I].
